## Repository Locator Gate

Before `git pull`, `git clone`, `git push`, update, sync, or cross-device
recovery, resolve the repository with `scripts/resolve-workflow-repo.ps1` when
available. A registry path is a candidate, not proof. Accept a path only after
`.git` and the expected Git remote identity are verified. If the
resolver reports `not_found`, `invalid`, or `ambiguous`, stop and show the
candidate paths instead of guessing.

Use `scripts/register-project.ps1` to add a project safely: run it once without
`-ConfirmWrite` to show a focused project summary, one representative
hardware/software/document detail when detected, and write plan, then rerun with
`-ConfirmWrite` only after approval.

## Resume Policy

- If `personal-state/ACTIVE_WORK.md` names an active work item, resume it
  first.
- If the prompt names a project, the named project overrides the latest active
  work item.
- If no active work exists and no project is named, scan recent work-item files,
  non-placeholder registry entries, recent Git activity, and recently modified
  local skills before asking for a target.
- Clone repositories on demand; do not mirror project contents into this hub.
- Keep imported reference skills and tutorials separate from owned projects.
